WEBVTT

00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:08,900
Hello everybody, this is Dr. Connors and this Zoom session, this recording, it's going

00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:17,780
to be about a serious spiritual matter when we come to wanting to be healed, that I think

00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:26,420
we need to address and just keep our focus to make sure that we keep our focus on the right

00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,420
things.

00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:32,380
We all want healing when we're sick, we have cancer, we have serious disease, we have

00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:41,900
Lyme, we have ALS, Parkinson's and all sorts of problems in this world. And we can ask

00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:49,020
serious questions and I think you're called to do that. When we go through the grieving process

00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:58,380
of understanding that we are mortal and our life is not to be lived completely on this

00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:03,260
earth, it gets a little scary, but where in our 20s we think we're going to live forever.

00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:12,620
And as we get older and we start having serious diagnoses, then that reality hits in. And many times

00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:17,580
we turn to God and that's a blessing. We're supposed to turn to God in times of crisis.

00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:22,940
But we have to be careful that we don't turn to God just to get what we want.

00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:31,020
Yes, we're supposed to ask for what we want and the Bible is very clear that you don't receive

00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:38,300
because you don't ask. But it's also very clear that we're supposed to ask with the right heart

00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:45,900
and we're supposed to accept God's answer. Paul made it very clear that he asked for his

00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:52,460
thorn of his side to be taken away three times, he said, which I find it kind of funny because

00:01:52,460 --> 00:02:03,100
I probably asked for my thorns to be taken away 575 times at least. And I don't fully understand

00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:09,580
that passage why he would only ask three times. But maybe it was three different periods of his life

00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:16,620
where he was intense prayer about whatever that thorn be in illness, a deformity, whatever it is,

00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:22,780
we don't know. And he was intensely in prayer and got the answer from God that it wasn't going to

00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:27,820
be taken away and he let it go for a period of time and then took it up another period of time.

00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:33,820
And there's a time and a season for everything and we're called to do that. And we need to be

00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:41,660
fervent in our prayer and fervent in our asking. And I think we need to ask for healing. I'm praying

00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:49,100
for healing for all of you and for myself on a daily basis. But we have to keep it in balance.

00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:55,820
First of all, biblically is healing promised. We can pull up verses all through the Bible where

00:02:55,820 --> 00:03:03,340
healing was promised to a certain person, to a certain people group and to us as believers as whole.

00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:13,020
So healing is for us in the new covenant. God did come to heal all our wounds and all our diseases.

00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:20,220
But that doesn't mean that they're going to be healed this side of heaven. If that was true,

00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:24,940
every believer from the New Testament on would still be alive. And that's not true.

00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:36,940
All the apostles suffered and died for his sake. Many were brutally bartered. And to think that we

00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:47,420
have the right to not go down that same pathway is pompous, arrogant and just absolutely foolish.

00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:57,180
If we want to serve our Savior, we need to be willing to die in the flesh just as our Savior did.

00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:05,020
Paul said, oh, that I may encompass the same sufferings that my Lord Jesus did, that he could

00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:13,500
know him more fully. And that's going to be our desire of our heart as well, not that we run around by

00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:23,260
like Vasekis wanting to be tortured for God. But if we're not willing to suffer for his namesake,

00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:29,020
we have to really question where we are with our relationship with him. Though we're supposed to ask

00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:35,100
for a healing, we're supposed to be praying for healing and praying for all the things that we need

00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:43,580
in our life, they cannot be more important than our relationship with him. And as I write in

00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:51,980
my book, Kids or Kid Kill You, if you're already dead, our first and foremost prayer has got to be

00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:57,660
asking God to put his desires in our heart. What do you want me to pray for, Lord?

00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:06,700
Maybe God's got me with this sickness so that I'll get out my knees and get closer to him and ask

00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:14,940
him what he wants me to pray for instead of just praying selfish prayers. I'm always speaking for

00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:20,940
myself, this is just my walk and I can encourage you through my walk about telling you what to do,

00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:27,340
but I know that's how God deals with me. He gives me sufferings to break me. He gives me

00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:36,140
sufferings to deal with strongholds in my life so that I can turn it over to him more readily because

00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:43,820
I fall every day. I think I can do it myself every day and through my sufferings is how I learn

00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:53,660
obedience. Through my struggles I learn obedience. And that is my prayer every day, Lord, what do you

00:05:53,660 --> 00:06:00,060
need me to pray for? What do you need me to do? How do you need me to pray? Who do you need me to ask

00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:11,100
for help for? Because this isn't about me. Life is not about me. Life is not about me. Be healthy and

00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:17,260
rollerblading when I'm 85 years old and living this wonderful life. What good is that? What's the

00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:24,860
importance of that? That is not supposed to be our God in our life and that's what we have to

00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:33,420
be careful about. We need to be asking what is the will of God for me? God, what do you want for me

00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:43,020
to do? If I've surrendered myself to be His, it's not about me anymore. That's done. It's not about

00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:51,340
me anymore. I've surrendered myself to Him. And if I have truly surrendered myself to Him and it's a

00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:57,100
daily basis, it's a daily walk. I understand that. It doesn't just happen one second in time. That's

00:06:57,100 --> 00:07:06,540
what sanctification is all about. Is Him chiseling away the rough edges of me to mold me and shape me

00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:16,700
daily more to be like the image of His Son and it's a painful process. And I need to be willing to

00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:21,420
go through that pain. It's easy to say that, but when I'm in the middle of that pain, I need to be

00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:29,820
reminded of that. So that is what the will of God is for me. Not for me to live to be 95 years old

00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:36,060
and have us wonderful life and have a 401k and be able to golf every day. It's wonderful if you could

00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:41,740
do that. Don't get me wrong. But you need to be asking, is that the will of God for me? How can

00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:47,740
I serve you? How can I get to the end to hear those faithful words? Well done, good and faithful

00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:55,500
servant. That's my goal. And I hope that's your goal too. And that's where we have to be careful.

00:07:55,500 --> 00:08:02,300
And I have to say some sharp words because healing or anything else can be idolatry.

00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:11,340
If my whole focus in life is to get something from God, that's idolatry. And I know those are

00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:18,700
tough words and I know that might slap somebody in the face, but let it. Our purpose has to be

00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:26,620
free from idolatry. Our purpose has to be Lord, I'm your tool. Use me. However you want to use me,

00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:33,580
whether you want to make me go through horrible things and suffer because somebody's watching me

00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:39,980
and somebody's going to be set free because of that, Lord, let it be your will. I remember,

00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:45,260
I think I've told you this story before. We were missionaries down in Mexico for a short period of time

00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:55,500
and we had wet self-financed. We sold everything that we had. This is back when we were in our early 30s.

00:08:56,380 --> 00:09:03,340
And we played a stay in three years, but see the deed down there. We taught at a Bible school

00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:10,460
and an orphanage in Bolteray, Mexico. And we ended up building a dormitory there and I taught

00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:19,260
at the Bible school for a year the Covenant of God. And we also worked in the Shanty towns,

00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:25,980
down in Mexico, in the borders and in the Shanty towns in Bolteray. And we used to go back with our

00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:31,340
suburban. We had four kids at the time. We used to drive back and we registered as missionaries with

00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:37,020
some wonderful organizations on the other side of the border. Bolteray is about three to half hours

00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:43,580
in from the border of Texas, South Texas. And we used to pick up about every weekend or every other

00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:50,380
weekend. We used to pick up and load our suburban full of stuff that we were given by feed the children

00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:57,020
international and things that they were given by different corporations and stuff that we could give

00:09:57,020 --> 00:10:01,820
away and that we could be a blessing to the people of the Shanty towns. And we used to pull it

00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:07,580
into the Shanty towns with our truck and I used to say with my broken Spanish, everybody light up and

00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:12,300
we would share a message of Jesus Christ and we would give people things and we would go around to

00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:17,980
their little places and talk to them about the Lord as best we could. And they were also gracious

00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:23,660
because they were all want to be Americans and so everybody was so kind to us and we'd ever felt

00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:30,220
even in the worst situations that we were threatened or we were a danger in any way that we probably were,

00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:36,220
we just trusted the Lord that was going to take care of us. But I remember coming back from there

00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:41,660
after we left after a little over a year we were down there. We just completely ran out of funds and

00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:46,460
we could not raise money to stay down there anymore and we had really no choice but to come back.

00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:56,460
And my wife and two youngest had my father flew them back up from South Texas and I was driving back

00:10:56,460 --> 00:11:04,380
with my two older daughters. They were their early teens or a little bit younger at the time.

00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:14,300
And we had nothing. We had zero money, not one penny left. And I was pulling our suburban and I had

00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:21,260
just enough gas money to get home. And we had rented a U-Haul, a little TD U-Haul trailer. We were

00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:26,140
pulling that because we had purchased some mattresses and a bunk bed down there. We didn't want to

00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:33,660
give that up so we brought that back with us. So all our worldly possessions were the suburban in

00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:40,140
this little U-Haul trailer. Pull it back and I just remember the girls were sleeping and I was

00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:44,460
just crying out to the Lord because we didn't have a job. We didn't have, I didn't have my

00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:52,140
care. Practic license that couldn't practice anymore. I had given that up and it's crying out to the

00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:58,860
Lord because I felt like the best we could describe all our work down there was that we were putting

00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:06,540
drops of water into a bucket that had no bottom. That's what I felt like. What did we do

00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:13,820
anything to make a difference? We toiled and worked day and night and I just felt like we didn't do

00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:18,540
anything to make a difference. And it was one of those moments that I felt like I really heard from

00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:26,700
the Holy Spirit directly to my heart. And he said, if I would have had you do this all over again

00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:37,420
for just one person would you do it? And that was a ginormous slap in the face to me because it was

00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:49,020
a revelation that God would send his son to go to the cross for just me or just one person and suffer

00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:55,900
everything that he suffered to take on the sins of the world for my salvation alone. If it was only

00:12:55,900 --> 00:13:03,740
for me why wouldn't I do that for him for just one person? And it's just a revelation that it's not

00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:10,940
about me. It's not about my stuff. It's not about my purpose and it's so easy especially in America

00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:19,900
to become so idolatrous to things and to thinking that we have the right to even health who says I have

00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:29,580
the right to health. A kind of warped sense of understanding is that we have the right to health.

00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:36,860
It is by a miracle of God that I am breathing today. There's a miracle that my heart is beating.

00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:43,180
It is said to be thankful for that I'm widened because oh my gosh I might have two months

00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:47,420
to live or eight months to live or two years to live. You could never have been promised two

00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:55,340
seconds to live. Praise God that he's given me today and yet we worry so much about tomorrow.

00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:04,040
Jesus said to Peter let the days old troubles be enough for today and I need to learn that.

00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:13,880
The problem is really honestly it's who we put our faith in that makes a difference. The problem is

00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:20,200
most of the time I have my faith in what? In me getting better that's what my faith is. My faith is in

00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:26,680
me carrying cancer. My faith is in this right-fishing working or my nutrition working. My faith is in

00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:33,480
is in my relationships being good. My faith is that my 401K is still healthy and that the economy is

00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:43,540
going to stay up. That's the wrong thing to have our faith in. It's a faith in who? That's who we have

00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:50,100
to have our faith in. It's our faith in Jesus Christ that he is enough. There's a story in the

00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:58,340
Bible of a woman who is bleeding for a decade or so and sick and it has been to her life savings going

00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:04,740
to doctors and Jesus was walking through a crowd being touched by everybody reaching out,

00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:10,740
wanting something from him. Jesus, Jesus, heal me, heal me. The apostles I can imagine were pushing

00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:16,660
the p- crowds back and a woman crawled underneath everybody and thought if I could just touch his

00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:26,660
garment because he has everything I need. He is everything I need and she rubbed her hand along

00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:34,580
his garment as he walked by and healing went out from him and healed her. An crazy thing in the

00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:41,700
midst of this crowd. Jesus turns around to his apostles and says who touched me? I'm sure the

00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:48,580
apostles are like, are you freaking out of your mind? Lord, I mean everybody's touching you were smashed

00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:53,860
in this crowd. Everybody's screaming. What do you mean who touched you? What do you mean who touched

00:15:53,860 --> 00:16:00,420
you? Somebody touched me. Somebody touched me and he turns around. Who touched me? Who touched me?

00:16:00,420 --> 00:16:06,260
And here, left of the ground, this is woman crouched, looking up, shy,

00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:16,500
uninvited wondering, am I going to get you all that? She said, Lord, it was I. And he said,

00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:24,100
your faith has healed you. Does that mean your faith in being healed? Does that mean your faith in

00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:34,820
being cured? I don't believe so. I believe it was her faith in Jesus Christ. Her faith that he was

00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:45,380
everything he was all she needed whether she was going to be healed or not. She was all he was all she

00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:52,660
needed. And that's where we need to be. God is all I need whether I get healed or I don't get healed.

00:16:52,660 --> 00:17:01,140
It's not about this world. This is not my home. I want to go home, I long for eternity. I long to

00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:09,700
spend eternity in heaven just getting to know my Savior more and more forever and ever and ever and ever.

00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:17,620
That's how vast the knowledge of God is. None of us could even understand or grasp the depth

00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:25,300
with the breath of the knowledge of God that we're going to gain in eternity. That's what I

00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:31,620
long for. Yes, do I want to be healed? Sure. Do I want to spend some time with my grandkids and my

00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:39,540
children and my wife? Absolutely. But not more than I want to spend with my Savior. And if it is ever

00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:46,260
more than I want to spend with my Savior, they are an idol in my life. And Lord, may that never be.

00:17:48,470 --> 00:17:55,350
That needs to be our prayer. Lord, make you all I need, Heavenly Father.

00:17:56,230 --> 00:18:04,150
Just whatever you need to put me through so that you are all I need and you are my desire

00:18:04,150 --> 00:18:11,750
of my heart. Lord, we thank You in Jesus' name. Amen.

